# CodeChecker skip list for kernel (device) code analysis, used with
# --drop-reports-from-skipped-files so these paths are dropped from both
# analysis and reporting. Exclusion-only: anything not listed is analyzed.
# Why not an allow-list, and why this rather than HeaderFilterRegex, in
# tech_reports/code-indexing/kernel-clang-tidy.md.
#
# The generated JIT glue under the kernel cache is analyzed on purpose. Do not
# add it back without reading that report first.

# Upstream toolchain: pinned SFPI release and the host libc/libstdc++ used for
# the analysis parse. Not fixable in this repo.
-/opt/tenstorrent/sfpi/*
-/usr/*
